Run away, Baron Corp.

263
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,300
And leave you? Yes.

264
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,129
We'll stay here and fight.

265
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:13,020
You gotta keep Nico Robin safe.

266
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:22,140
All right, we'll go, but
be careful. We'll be fine.

267
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,594
We're not so helpless.

268
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,162
Come on, Robin.

269
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,597
You heard what they said, right?

270
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:29,840
They'll be killed.

271
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:34,297
That's precisely why we must go.

272
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:37,180
We cannot allow their
sacrifice to be in vain.

273
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:59,177
I can't believe they're defeating
the Mink Warriors so easily.

274
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:02,025
Whoever those men are,
they're terribly strong.

275
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:03,210
CP0.

276
00:20:03,293 --> 00:20:04,828
They're a Cipher pole unit.

277
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:07,380
We saw them before, back in Dressrosa.

278
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,537
They're government officers, right?

279
00:20:09,620 --> 00:20:10,796
Intelligence agents?

280
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,666
But what are they doing here?

281
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:15,717
And why are they looking
for you at a time like this?

282
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:19,300
I couldn't say, but we're
facing the worst case scenario.

283
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,880
That much is apparent at least. What?

284
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:26,540
Cape is the top-ranked
unit in all of Cypher-Pole.

285
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:30,825
And the masked agents are the
most dangerous, even amongst them.

286
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:36,213
It seems that our escape
options are a little bare-bound.

287
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:37,440
Yo-ho-ho!

288
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:38,779
Well, look at you.

289
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:39,970
Now, come on.

290
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:42,002
Let's get you to somewhere safe.

291
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:43,560
Time to fly!

292
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,420
Where are you?

293
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,060
Jaggy!

294
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:56,637
This is a disaster...

295
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,800
Jaggy!

296
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:06,240
Um, excuse me?

297
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,960
Could you help me?

298
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,560
Whoever you are?

299
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,420
Judge used to talk about this.

300
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:14,297
Please, I have nothing to do with this!

301
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,237
I'm just a geisha from the Capitol!

302
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:18,860
He wanted to create the perfect soldier.

303
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:19,970
Shut up!

304
00:21:20,053 --> 00:21:22,960
With incredible strength
and a heart of ice.

305
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:26,300
Powerful and merciless. Shut up!

306
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,777
I just want to go home!

307
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,117
Can you help me get out of here?

308
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:33,777
Don't pretend you're not excited to show
off that germ of blood in your veins!

309
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:35,389
I'm not like them, dammit!

310
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:37,980
I'M HUMAN!

311
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:41,790
What?

312
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:54,960
Are you okay, miss? Stay back!

313
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:58,120
Don't come any closer!

314
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:11,000
I need help!

315
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:15,140
Osume, what happened?

316
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:16,620
You're bleeding!

317
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:18,140
I did this to you!

318
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:21,080
Miss, are you alright?

319
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:22,321
Let me help you.

320
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:26,199
How dare you attack this poor girl!

321
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,860
You call yourself a man!

322
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:30,157
Please, you've got this wrong.

323
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:32,220
I would never... Excuses!

324
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:34,677
You're fighting on the
side of Wano, aren't you?

325
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:35,820
Of course I am.

326
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:38,651
Then you're doing this to your own people.

327
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:39,700
Listen to me.

328
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,797
I don't know what happened to her.

329
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,233
I just showed up and...

330
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:46,337
I didn't...

331
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,700
I didn't do anything.

332
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:52,657
I didn't lay a finger on her.

333
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,017
I was just.

334
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:55,500
I don't know.

335
00:22:57,620 --> 00:22:59,697
If you're so innocent, why did she run?

336
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:01,317
I don't want to hear a word.

337
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:02,677
It doesn't matter what you say.

338
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:04,277
We're trying to hide now.

339
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,217
Leave before someone finds this place.

340
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:09,777
Monsters who beat up innocent
girls are not welcome here.

341
00:23:09,860 --> 00:23:11,857
I swear this wasn't me.

342
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:14,037
I promised you. Shut up.

343
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:15,540
Get out of here.

344
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:18,290
Go!

345
00:23:18,380 --> 00:23:19,737
Haven't you done enough?

346
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:21,877
Don't ever show your face here again!

347
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:22,790
Stop it!

348
00:23:22,873 --> 00:23:23,780
Go on, leave!

349
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,177
Please, I wouldn't...

350
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:29,680
I couldn't...

351
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,060
This isn't happening.

352
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,420
I would never lay a hand on a lady.

353
00:23:44,420 --> 00:23:45,620
Hey, Jermaboy!

354
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,120
Found you!

355
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:52,500
What you doing over here?

356
00:23:52,780 --> 00:23:56,074
Hate to break it to you, but
the pleasure hall's closed.

357
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:57,250
No way.

358
00:23:57,333 --> 00:23:59,261
That's the last thing I would do.

359
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,640
I could never hurt a woman.

360
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:03,130
Could I?

361
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:07,080
They feed a woman unconscious.

362
00:24:08,820 --> 00:24:12,173
Everything you guys represent
goes against my principles.

363
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:15,644
You're telling me I'm
going to end up like them?

364
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:16,750
Yeah.

365
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:19,064
My body isn't tingling anymore.

366
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:21,249
Maybe it already happened.

367
00:24:22,080 --> 00:24:26,315
I was caught up in my thoughts when
I ran into that girl in the hallway.

368
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:32,520
It took me a second to notice her, and
then she went flying, and she was bleeding.

369
00:24:33,660 --> 00:24:35,954
She looked at me with fear in her eyes.

370
00:24:38,420 --> 00:24:39,250
Dammit.

371
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:42,640
Hey, Luffy.

372
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:46,831
What kind of man do you want on your crew?

373
00:24:48,460 --> 00:24:52,540
An unreliable dreamer like me,
who's afraid of his own power,

374
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,529
who's helpless every
time he faces a woman?

375
00:24:56,780 --> 00:24:59,317
Or a warrior of science who can beat up a

376
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:01,617
monster like this
without a second thought,

377
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:05,820
who has a heart of ice and a
will of steel that never fails?

378
00:25:08,420 --> 00:25:11,596
Which would be more useful
to the King of the Pirates?

379
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:16,480
I need you on my crew, Saadji!

380
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:17,800
Without you!

381
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,760
I don't know what'll happen
from here on out, but...

382
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,137
Is that the Germa suit?

383
00:25:27,220 --> 00:25:28,514
Are you gonna wear it?

384
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:31,240
I know what I have to do.

385
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,680
When I put this suit on,

386
00:25:34,460 --> 00:25:38,060
it awakened a power that's been
inside me since I was born.

387
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:41,100
I can't do anything to change that.

388
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:43,760
Sounds like you finally get it.

389
00:25:43,860 --> 00:25:46,160
Now, suit up, Jermaboy!

390
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:50,500
What I can do is put
an end to all of this.

391
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:01,880
I need you on my crew, Sanji!

392
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:08,180
Without you, without you, I'll
never be king of the pirates!

393
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:13,457
It's over.

394
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:16,477
I'm choosing my own fate.

395
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:19,437
What the hell are you doing?

396
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:20,477
I said put it on.

397
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:21,620
Not destroy it.

398
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:26,800
Goodbye, Jeremiah.

399
00:26:30,180 --> 00:26:31,557
Goodbye, women's back.

400
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:36,640
I'm gonna finish this
fight on my own terms.

401
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:49,910
Huh?

402
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:53,250
Collect.

403
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:54,640
What the hell?

404
00:26:54,900 --> 00:26:56,429
When do I have this thing?

405
00:26:59,860 --> 00:27:02,180
Who's calling me at a time like this?

406
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:03,800
I'm busy!

407
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:08,317
I was afraid you might be
dying in a ditch somewhere.

408
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:12,057
So I snuck that snail on
you as a safety precaution.

409
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:13,720
I'm not dying, you idiot!

410
00:27:15,620 --> 00:27:17,100
Could you leave me alone?

411
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:19,800
Listen, this won't take long.

412
00:27:24,540 --> 00:27:26,140
I know we got this.

413
00:27:26,420 --> 00:27:29,185
We're beating the beast
pirates no matter what.

414
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,940
Yeah, of course we are!

415
00:27:37,540 --> 00:27:43,500
But after the battle, there's a chance
I might not be in my right mind anymore.

416
00:27:49,180 --> 00:27:52,220
If that happens, then kill me. What?

417
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:09,700
He's still there?

418
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:14,660
Yeah, I got it.

419
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:17,117
No problem.

420
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:19,440
I'll kill you, just like you asked.

421
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:25,624
I don't get what your problem is, but at
least I got something to look forward to.

422
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:33,420
So until then, don't you dare die on me.

423
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:36,080
I appreciate it.

424
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:43,870
lick.

425
00:28:43,953 --> 00:28:44,880
Hey, where'd you go?

426
00:28:45,380 --> 00:28:46,717
You got invisibility tech?

427
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,741
Bet daddy gave you that too, huh?

428
00:28:50,900 --> 00:28:53,340
I don't need you adding fuel to the fire.

429
00:28:58,520 --> 00:29:00,840
Because I'm already burning up!

430
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:07,240
I'M SENDING YOU STRAIGHT TO HELL!

431
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:14,220
HELL MEMORIES!
